  "rationale": "The batch repeatedly uses common object nouns after determiners, including apples after an initial “The” and pears after “the”. Existing noun rules already favor some specific verb-and-determiner contexts, but they provide weak support for a bare determiner context, as shown by the very low probability of apples after “The”. Add modest suffix rules for the recurring object nouns rather than copying a full story or asserting that a determiner uniquely predicts a noun. Adjectives and other valid continuations should remain possible; these rules may be less helpful when an adjective is expected next, so their weights are deliberately moderate. No head change is needed because the prefix’s determiner is directly available.",
